# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the Linux suite under `make asan`.
#
# PipeWire loads its client modules with dlopen when a context is created and
# dlcloses them when it is destroyed. What they allocate — on the caller's
# thread through pw_context_load_module, or on PipeWire's own loop thread
# through libspa-support — is still referenced from the module's static data
# at that point, and once the module is unloaded LSan can no longer see those
# references: every report is "<unknown module>" frames under one of these
# two. None has a mynah frame; checked 2026-09-23 with malloc_context_size=100.
leak:pw_context_load_module
leak:libspa-support.so
